%% Connection lifecycle - the confirmed sequence, with every unknown marked.
%% Dashed steps are inferred from control flow; they were NOT observed running.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant Vpn as VpnService
    participant NetM as NetworkManagement
    participant V2Ray as V2RayService / SshService
    participant Proc as ProcessRunner
    participant Tun as tun2socks / v2ray
    participant Tap as TAP-Windows adapter
    participant OS as Host routing + DNS

    User->>Vpn: connect()
    Note over Vpn: CONFIRMED - all bodies decoded

    Vpn->>NetM: enumerate adapters (WMI)
    Note right of NetM: CONFIRMED<br/>SELECT * FROM Win32_NetworkAdapter<br/>WHERE Manufacturer = 'TAP-Windows Provider V9'
    NetM-->>Vpn: TAP adapter handle

    Vpn->>Vpn: resolve config from DefaultPreferences
    Note right of Vpn: CONFIRMED - 39 methods, literals recovered

    alt V2Ray mode
        Vpn->>V2Ray: build v2ray config
        Note right of V2Ray: CONFIRMED - 46-method V2RayConfig<br/>full JSON key vocabulary
        V2Ray->>Proc: write profile.json, launch v2ray
    else SOCKS / proxy mode
        Vpn->>Proc: launch tun2socks with recovered argv
        Note right of Proc: CONFIRMED - argument template recovered<br/>--tundev "tap0901:..." --socks-server-addr 127.0.0.1:&lt;port&gt;
    else SSH mode
        Vpn->>Proc: launch plink
        Note right of Proc: INFERRED - settings keys present,<br/>exact argv UNRESOLVED
    end

    Proc-->>Vpn: child process handle
    Vpn->>OS: add routes, set interface DNS 10.4.2.1
    Note right of OS: CONFIRMED
    Vpn->>OS: remove saved default-gateway entry
    Note right of OS: CONFIRMED<br/>see NF-03
    Tap-->>User: traffic flows
    Note over Tap: CONFIRMED - adapter and address assignment<br/>observed in recovered configuration only

    rect rgb(255, 251, 235)
        Note over Vpn,OS: UNRESOLVED - what happens between<br/>"process started" and "gateway removed".<br/>No runtime observation was made, so the<br/>ordering of these steps is inferred,<br/>not demonstrated.
    end

    User->>Vpn: disconnect()
    Vpn->>Proc: kill helper process
    Vpn->>OS: remove installed routes
    Vpn->>OS: **restore saved default gateway**
    Note right of OS: CONFIRMED on the orderly path<br/>- single restoration site
    Vpn->>Tap: release TAP configuration

    rect rgb(255, 235, 238)
        Note over User,OS: UNRESOLVED - abnormal termination.<br/>Nothing guarantees restoration after a crash,<br/>a kill, or a power loss.<br/>See NF-03.
    end